 about a thousand feet. At 6:40, at F5, it hit the Golden Spur mobile home park on the west edge of Andover, where the town's only siren failed to sound: 13 of the 39 people who stayed in their homes were killed; 200 more survived in the park's underground shelter. It reached its widest, about 0.4 mile, three miles farther on, passed half a mile from Towanda and lifted five miles north of El Dorado at 7:14. 17 dead, 225 injured, 46 miles.","segments":[{"county":"Sedgwick","state":"Kansas","ef":"EF5","width":440,"miles":24.0,"from":40320,"to":40320,"deaths":4,"inj":75},{"county":"Butler","state":"Kansas","ef":"EF5","width":700,"miles":22.0,"from":42900,"to":42900,"deaths":13,"inj":150}]},{"name":"Garfield, OK","ef":"EF3","start":40500,"end":41220,"coords":[[-97.77,36.4],[-97.67,36.43]],"lengthMi":6.0,"widthYd":350.0,"inj":0,"fat":0,"state":"OK","geometry":"endpoints","timing":"estimated","segments":[{"county":"Garfield","state":"Oklahoma","ef":"EF3","width":350,"miles":6.0,"from":40500,"to":40500,"deaths":0,"inj":0}]},{"name":"Sedgwick\u2013Harvey, KS","ef":"EF1","start":41100,"end":43020,"coords":[[-97.38,37.83],[-97.37438,37.88063],[-97.37063,37.90687],[-97.36688,37.92563],[-97.36125,37.94625],[-97.35,37.98]],"lengthMi":16.0,"widthYd":50.0,"inj":0,"fat":0,"state":"KS","geometry":"segments","timing":"the survey's county-by-county clock times","widths":[50,47,33,23,12,10],"times":[41100,41303,41408,41610,42141,43020],"sources":["NOAA Storm Events Database \u2014 county-by-county survey records"],"segments":[{"county":"Sedgwick","state":"Kansas","ef":"EF1","width":50,"miles":11.0,"from":41100,"to":41100,"deaths":0,"inj":0},{"county":"Harvey","state":"Kansas","ef":"EF1","width":10,"miles":5.0,"from":41460,"to":41460,"deaths":0,"inj":0}]},{"name":"Garfield, OK","ef":"EF0","start":41400,"end":41460,"coords":[[-97.6,36.43],[-97.5988,36.4311]],"lengthMi":0.1,"widthYd":20.0,"inj":0,"fat":0,"state":"OK","geometry":"point","timing":"estimated","segments":[{"county":"Garfield"